          "summary": "Add a reasonableness standard to assignment consent and a written-notice requirement for successor assignments in Section 14.1.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] Section 14.1 requires the other party's consent to any assignment with no reasonableness standard, so consent to a permitted transaction (including where an acquirer is said to be a competitor) could be withheld arbitrarily. We have added the customary \"not unreasonably withheld\" standard and a written-notice requirement for successor assignments, which is our fallback position; the rest of the section is unchanged.",
